## The quick formula

**Boxes = ceil(Room area × (1 + waste%) ÷ box coverage)**

## Waste factor by lay pattern

| Pattern | Waste to add | When to use |
|---------|-------------|-------------|
| Straight lay (rows parallel to wall) | **+10%** | Most rooms |
| Diagonal lay (45° angle) | **+15%** | Feature floors, small rooms |
| Complex rooms (L-shape, many cuts) | **+15%** | Multiple doorways, unusual shapes |

## Boxes needed by room size (20 sq ft box, straight lay)

| Room size | Area | With 10% waste | Boxes needed |
|-----------|------|----------------|--------------|
| 8 × 10 ft | 80 sq ft | 88 sq ft | 5 boxes |
| 10 × 12 ft | 120 sq ft | 132 sq ft | 7 boxes |
| 12 × 12 ft | 144 sq ft | 158 sq ft | 8 boxes |
| 12 × 16 ft | 192 sq ft | 211 sq ft | 11 boxes |
| 16 × 20 ft | 320 sq ft | 352 sq ft | 18 boxes |

## Common box coverages

| Flooring type | Typical box coverage | Notes |
|---------------|---------------------|-------|
| Vinyl plank (LVP) | 20–23 sq ft | LifeProof, COREtec, Pergo |
| Laminate | 20–25 sq ft | Shaw, Pergo, Quick-Step |
| Engineered hardwood | 15–25 sq ft | Varies by board width |

**Always use the number printed on your specific box.** It varies by product.

## How to measure your room

1. Measure length × width in feet for rectangular rooms
2. For L-shaped rooms: break into two rectangles, measure each, add together
3. Subtract permanent fixtures (built-in cabinets, closets you won't floor)
4. Add your waste percentage

Use the [Flooring Calculator](/calculator/flooring) with the Irregular shape option for complex rooms.

